Dictionary data

The generated dictionary in data/dictionary uses the following sources under
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0).
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

- JMdict, by James William Breen and the Electronic Dictionary Research and
  Development Group (EDRDG). KanjiGraph extracts and normalizes spellings
  and readings from JMdict.
  https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project
  https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html
- JmdictFurigana data, by Doublevil, derived from JMdict. KanjiGraph uses
  the reading annotations to add furigana to dictionary entries.
  https://github.com/Doublevil/JmdictFurigana#licence
- similar-kanji.tsv, by Kanji Database (kanji-db.com). KanjiGraph converts
  the pairs into a lookup of visually similar kanji. See the upstream
  attribution for source data, including Yi Bai's IDS component data.
  https://kanji-db.com/en/data
  https://github.com/uball/kanji-db-data/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md

The resulting dictionary data are distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
